  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV/AIDS - Sao Tome and Principe (01-Jan-2017-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sao Tome and Principe, HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Sao Tome and Principe)This program has the following goals: To decrease the morbidity and mortality of People living with HIV/AIDS, vulnerable groups and Most-at-risk populations. The objectives of this program are: To eliminate mother-to-child transmission of HIV.  To increase the institutional capacity of the National AIDS Programme / Ministry of Health as well as Civil Society in order to respond to the HIV epidemic.  To reduce the morbidity, mortality and improve the quality of life of people living with HIV, their partners and families and support orphans..  To significantly reduce the sexual transmission of HIV infection in S&#xe3;o Tome and Principe</narrative>
  </description>
